# ${name} for ${business}

One IRA instance, made by `ira init` on ${date}. It answers with
${provider_note}.

| File | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `ira.yaml` | The settings: models, voice, port. No secrets. |
| `tools.py` | Two placeholder tools. Replace them with your own. |
| `data/` | Made on first start: `ira.db` (accounts, conversations, the audit log) and your tools' files. Back it up. |
| `.env` | Not made for you. Only for keys other than the server's AWS role; `chmod 600`. |

## Check and start

```bash
ira doctor --no-models   # config, data folder, port, tools, accounts: no calls
ira doctor               # the same, plus one tiny call to each model and voice
ira serve                # while no owner exists, prints a one-time setup link
```

Open the setup link to create the owner account and set the action PIN, then
run `ira doctor` again: it passes once the owner has a PIN.

## Make it yours

- Describe the business in `assistant.business` and `assistant.instructions`.
- Replace `find_notes` and `add_note` in `tools.py` with tools over your own
  data. Reads are `@tool`; changes are `@action`, and run only after a PIN.
- Run `ira doctor` after every change. It loads each tool module and says
  which tools it found, or why it failed.
